            <li><strong>Phase II: AI Agent Integration:</strong> Developing a smart "Digital <span class="highlight">constable</span>" AI. This agent will monitor environmental safety in real-time, acting as a vigilant guardian to warn the user of hazards (e.g., wet floors, moving vehicles, or broken sidewalks) via haptic vibrations or bone-conduction audio.</li>
            <li><strong>Phase III: User Pilot Study:</strong> Testing the hardware (smart glasses and haptic vests) within a controlled urban environment with a diverse cohort of participants with varying disability profiles.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>4. Expected Outcomes</h2>
        <p>We anticipate a significant reduction in "navigation anxiety" scores among participants. Success will be measured by:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Increased independence in unnavigated urban environments.</li>
            <li>Reduction in time taken to complete daily transit tasks.</li>
            <li>Increased subjective happiness and social participation levels reported through qualitative interviews.</li>
        </ol>
    </section>

